# Descriptions for niri binds that carry no hotkey-overlay-title.
#
# A titled bind supplies its own label to both the DMS cheatsheet and (still)
# niri's native overlay. An untitled one has nothing to show, so it is named
# here instead of being given a title -- a title would also add it to niri's
# fixed-order overlay, which is the thing Mod+Slash no longer opens.
#
# tooling/keybindings/build-cheatsheet asserts this file in both directions:
# every untitled, non-hidden bind must appear here, and every entry must name a
# bind that still exists. Adding a bind without describing it fails the build.
#
# Format: key|subcat|description
# An empty subcat inherits the `// -- Section --` heading the bind sits under
# in binds.kdl. An empty description is not allowed.

# --- Columns & window sizing --------------------------------------------
Mod+Q||Close the window
Mod+Comma||Pull the next window into this column
Mod+Period||Push this window out of the column
Mod+V||Float the window, or tile it again
Mod+W||Show the column as tabs instead of a stack
Mod+Shift+F||Fullscreen the window
Mod+Ctrl+F||Grow the window to the screen edges
Mod+Ctrl+C||Centre every visible column
Mod+Ctrl+R||Reset the window's height
Mod+Shift+Minus||Shrink the window's height by 10%
Mod+Shift+Equal||Grow the window's height by 10%

# --- Focus ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The letters and the arrows are the same binds; the arrow halves are titled.
Mod+H||Focus the column to the left
Mod+L||Focus the column to the right

# --- Move ----------------------------------------------------------------
Mod+Ctrl+H||Move the column left
Mod+Ctrl+L||Move the column right

# --- Workspaces ----------------------------------------------------------
Mod+U||Go to the workspace below
Mod+I||Go to the workspace above
Mod+Page_Down||Go to the workspace below
Mod+Page_Up||Go to the workspace above
Mod+Ctrl+U||Send the column to the workspace below
Mod+Ctrl+I||Send the column to the workspace above
Mod+Ctrl+Page_Down||Send the column to the workspace below
Mod+Ctrl+Page_Up||Send the column to the workspace above
Mod+Shift+U||Move this workspace down
Mod+Shift+I||Move this workspace up

# --- Monitors ------------------------------------------------------------
Mod+Shift+H||Focus the monitor to the left
Mod+Shift+J||Focus the monitor below
Mod+Shift+K||Focus the monitor above
Mod+Shift+L||Focus the monitor to the right
Mod+Shift+Ctrl+H||Send the column to the monitor left
Mod+Shift+Ctrl+J||Send the column to the monitor below
Mod+Shift+Ctrl+K||Send the column to the monitor above
Mod+Shift+Ctrl+L||Send the column to the monitor right

# --- System & utilities --------------------------------------------------
Mod+Escape|System & utilities|Stop an app from swallowing shortcuts

# --- Scroll --------------------------------------------------------------
Mod+WheelScrollDown||Wheel: next workspace
Mod+WheelScrollUp||Wheel: previous workspace
Mod+WheelScrollRight||Wheel: next column
Mod+WheelScrollLeft||Wheel: previous column
Mod+Shift+WheelScrollDown||Wheel: next column
Mod+Shift+WheelScrollUp||Wheel: previous column
Mod+Ctrl+WheelScrollDown||Wheel: send the column down a workspace
Mod+Ctrl+WheelScrollUp||Wheel: send the column up a workspace
Mod+Ctrl+WheelScrollRight||Wheel: move the column right
Mod+Ctrl+WheelScrollLeft||Wheel: move the column left
Mod+Ctrl+Shift+WheelScrollDown||Wheel: move the column right
Mod+Ctrl+Shift+WheelScrollUp||Wheel: move the column left

# --- Media & display -----------------------------------------------------
XF86AudioRaiseVolume||Volume up
XF86AudioLowerVolume||Volume down
XF86AudioMute||Mute the speakers
XF86AudioMicMute||Mute the microphone
XF86AudioPlay||Play or pause
XF86AudioNext||Next track
XF86AudioPrev||Previous track
XF86MonBrightnessUp||Brighter screen
XF86MonBrightnessDown||Dimmer screen

# --- Screenshots ---------------------------------------------------------
Ctrl+Print||Screenshot the whole screen
Alt+Print||Screenshot the focused window

# --- Binds DMS owns outright ---------------------------------------------
# A leading + marks an addition rather than a description. These live only in
# the DMS-generated ~/.config/niri/dms/binds.kdl, which is machine-generated and
# not in this repo, so nothing here can parse them -- but they are real keys on
# a running session and the sheet is meant to be complete.
#
# Only the ones we let DMS keep belong here. Mod+Y and Mod+Alt+L are DMS's too
# but local.kdl rebinds them hotkey-overlay-title=null to hide them, and that
# decision is honoured rather than undone.
+Mod+N|Launchers & apps|Notification centre
+Mod+Shift+N|Launchers & apps|Notepad
